I recently posted YASD post here, where I described a game where I got 
overconfident and got killed by Pestilence. This time I didn't get too 
cocky, in fact most of the time I was quite sure I'm not going to make it. I 
almost gave up a couple of times, but kept on trying. Remember, it's not 
over until the lady (of the invisible choir) sings...

As this is YAAP, I'll try to keep it brief. First few words of the early 
game though.

This was my second ascension, and first playing a samurai. It was my 48th 
try using a samurai (+ the ones i played using handheld device).

Start was unpromising. My pet dog died in a rock trap in the very beginning. 
I corroded my katana by being careless with a pudding/blob of some sort. 
That time I thought "what the heck, this game is not going anywhere, I can 
as well start quaffing from fountains". On Dlvl: 3 I quaffed from a fountain 
and a friendly water demon showed, giving me a blessed +3 SDSM.

At some point, later on, I found a Ring of Invisibility, and couldn't see 
myself which is annoying. So I needed see invisible intrinsic. I started 
quaffing from fountains again. This only resulted some of my things becoming 
cursed. One of them was my BoH. I was overtaxed, couldn't do a squat. And 
all my !oHW were in the bag... Dropping and looting the bag I lost a bunch 
of things, and got so annoyed I almost stopped playing. Next day things 
looked better again, I didn't lose any artifacts, and luckily my potions of 
holy water hadn't disappeared, so once I had emptied the bag I could uncurse 
it.

Soon after this, another incident followed which again was a result from 
quaffing fountains. A fountain had overflown and I carelessly stepped into 
the water. My BoH was not greased, so I lost furter more potions and scrolls 
(and maybe the candles too?). I had only recently learned about alchemy, but 
losing all those potions prevented me of trying it yet. When I found the 
vibrating square I realized I didn't have candles with me. Maybe they melted 
in the water (can that happen?), or maybe I mistakenly dropped and polypiled 
them into something else. So I had to climb 40+ levels up to the gnomish 
mines, then descend back down again.

I got through the Gehennom and planes, all the way to Astral plane. Since I 
had plenty of Wands of Death, I went on to dealing with Famine and 
Pestilence first. The plan worked, except that the right alter was in the 
center where Death was... Once I had reached the second altar, I had a 
bright idea of trying to convert the altar. This resulted a chaotic god 
getting very agry at me, throwing a ray of disintegration at me; I was 
disintegration resistant but my Cloak of Magic Resistance wasn't. Great, no 
magic resistance. That point I was pretty sure I'm not going to make it. I 
kept trying, however, and made my way through the mob. My two amulets of 
life saving were used up and I had no more of them. Since my guardian angel 
had ceased to exist, I put on a ring of conflict and that made moving a 
little easier. I reached Death and attacked it. I got strange message about 
skills increasing, and #enchance showed I was progressing in martial arts. 
WTH, I had just punched Death with my fists? Where did my +6 Tsurugi of 
Muramasa go? Luckily I had disenchanter-bitten +4 Excalibur which served me 
well to the end:

An invisible choir sings, and you are bathed in radiance...

